{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/462895-do-contracts-work-because-of-the-god-machine","id":462895,"title":"Do Contracts work because of the God-Machine?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-30T17:48:49-07:00","id":462895,"title":"Do Contracts work because of the God-Machine?","content":"Contracts work by inheriting greater than normal benefits due to occult agreements with aspects of reality and/or loopholes in this agreements that are exploited. Given that the God Machine is the arbiter and (arguably) the motive force behind how the universe works, is it reasonable to assume that the agreements are actually between something (Arcadia itself?) and the God Machine? If true, what are the implications of this? What's the metaphysical relationship between Contracts, Embeds and/or Exploits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T18:37:58-07:00","id":462972,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think that the Machine and the Wyrd are as different as night and day. One is a mechanical force that operates according to preset rules, and the other is a binding, chaotic webs of deals and favors and I'll let it slide this times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T19:09:46-07:00","id":462995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/462895-do-contracts-work-because-of-the-god-machine#post462895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contracts work by inheriting greater than normal benefits due to occult agreements with aspects of reality and/or loopholes in this agreements that are exploited. Given that the God Machine is the arbiter and (arguably) the motive force behind how the universe works, is it reasonable to assume that the agreements are actually between something (Arcadia itself?) and the God Machine? If true, what are the implications of this? What's the metaphysical relationship between Contracts, Embeds and/or Exploits?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> I swear, it's like Mage, except we're trying to impose a different cosmology. <i>Not everything is God Machine</i>.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine would <i>like</i> you to think that it's in charge (as much as a cold emotionless <i>thing</i> can like something), but the universe isn't being emulated on its hard drive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T19:35:53-07:00","id":463005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/462895-do-contracts-work-because-of-the-god-machine#post462895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contracts work by inheriting greater than normal benefits due to occult agreements with aspects of reality and/or loopholes in this agreements that are exploited. Given that the God Machine is the arbiter and (arguably) the motive force behind how the universe works, is it reasonable to assume that the agreements are actually between something (Arcadia itself?) and the God Machine? If true, what are the implications of this? What's the metaphysical relationship between Contracts, Embeds and/or Exploits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fuck no. A thousand times fuck no.<br /> <br /> There's a similarity in that there is the establishment of rules, but the Machine works on scientific principle pushed ahead of schedule-several embeds draw from psychological phenomenon as well as edge questions about quantum physics(Or hell, even quirks of normal physics). When it makes things like the movies, it's relying on the law of averages to produce an outcome that looks like the movies and then precludes all other options.pacts are a matter of re-programming the reality after the fact, which is why you have the odd tansferences of memories and the somewhat abrupt transfer of blessings.<br /> <br /> A Stranger or a changeling doesn't care about statistical probability and physics. To a fae, a one in a million shot is really a one in two-either it narratively happens or it doesn't*. This is because the Wyrd is a force of connection and context, metaphor and simile. When things happens like the movies around a goblin, it's because the fae are exploiting the Wyrd connecting these things together. THe contracts of the fae are the matter of establishing a connection with the Wyrd, and that's why it takes some time for those blessings to appear.<br /> <br /> *SPOILERS FOR MADOKA MAGICA!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In the show, they mention the odds of recovering a magical girl from their fate as a witch is one in a million. When Kyoko goes to save Sayaka, she fails. Later on, in the movie, without having her god-powers, it's up to Madoka to save Homura from herself as Homulily. Statistically speaking, she should fail, because the odds are still just as bad as before-in fact, they're worse. But we've already seen the NO answer come up, so the only answer left to explore narratively is YES-so that's what happens. It works, because a YES answer here opens up the door for more conflict(Essentially making it a YES BUT answer). In the end though, as far as saving witches and turning them back to magical girls, it should always more or less be impossible to do, but in reality, it's fifty fifty, because it's Either a NO or a YES.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T20:39:38-07:00","id":463049,"title":"","content":"Also, having literally just read Chapter One of Rites of Spring <i>last week</i>, I think it's a safe bet that the magic whose motifs resonate with nature and emotion aren't the preserve of the entity whose motifs resonate with dispassionate machinery.<br /> <br /> (Attempts to compare the variably-litigious word-bond of Other-worldly pledgecraft with the enshrined-in-material-record chartering of Unchained pactwork will be laughed out of the room.)<br /> <br /> The irony here is that I <i>have </i>wondered abound the potential comparability of Embeds to Contracts\u2026 but those are the Contracts from <i>Summoners</i>, which are sublet Paradox-free supernatural powers with a raw Attribute + Skill pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T00:51:27-07:00","id":463188,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I suspect that the god-machine doesn't care for changelings over much- they can see the future, manipulate the future like a story, have connection to the world of dreams were real world logic doesn't matter, and their magic works by over riding the laws of physics with the laws of narrative causality.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:01:54-07:00","id":463851,"title":"","content":"Note: My proposal is less &quot;Contacts = Embeds&quot; and more &quot;When whatever entity(s) sat down and puzzled out the agreements that would eventually allow for Contracts, the God Machine was an important figure at the table and either facilitated or allowed many / all of those agreements to be made in such a way that they work in the God Machine's world.&quot; Or, &quot;fae Magic works in the God Machine's world because the God Machine, for whatever reason, at one point said it was okay.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:22:31-07:00","id":463872,"title":"","content":"Considering the Machine is a &quot;No Gods before me&quot; kind of thing, I find the second improbable.<br /> <br /> THe former doesn't allow for the various metaphysics to work like they do given the Machine's own set of laws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:39:38-07:00","id":463952,"title":"","content":"I'd say they are totally unrelated.<br /> <br /> I don't think given the option the God-Machine would want Gentry or Changelings around at all, since they have powers to force a narrative upon reality and otherwise cheat a good deal. Embeds are subroutines created by the God-Machine in reality, or possibly simply accessed. I don't think they are the same thing at all.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine is a thing, and a major thing, in reality, but it is not <i>the</i> thing, nor is it the world itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T16:46:23-07:00","id":464014,"title":"","content":"Ultimately it is &quot;as the ST decide&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally? I'd say a big NO! It gets really tiresome every time a new Splat/Metaplot arrive they try to stick their viewpoints to other splats, ESPECIALLY Changeling (Both Dreaming &amp; Lost).<br /> <br /> I don't think there is that many Changeling players going on other forums, saying that the God-Machine is a Fae more active in the world, Vampires are human who contracted some kind of diseases from the Edge, Werewolves were originally Beast Changeling who have a contract with the Umbra etc...<br /> <br /> It is just as true as the God-Machine being behind the Wyrd or the Mage thingie about Arcadia.<br /> <br /> I really prefer when everything stay separated &amp; no one got a final answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T20:24:56-07:00","id":464225,"title":"","content":"Personal preference is they achieve the same goals in different ways. Like mac vs pc they are comparable but under the hood the how is different. <br /> <br /> That head cannon came from debating with st and trying to weave all the lines together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T23:38:38-07:00","id":464344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/462895-do-contracts-work-because-of-the-god-machine?p=462995#post462995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> <br /> I swear, it's like Mage, except we're trying to impose a different cosmology. <i>Not everything is God Machine</i>.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine would <i>like</i> you to think that it's in charge (as much as a cold emotionless <i>thing</i> can like something), but the universe isn't being emulated on its hard drive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage isn't nearly this bad. <br /> <br /> But then, Mage isn't being put into the WoD core rulebook, either; it's no wonder so many people seem to think the God-Machine is the center of the WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T23:49:33-07:00","id":464351,"title":"","content":"A shame the Nockers from Changeling the Dreaming aren't still around to boss the God Machine into submission.<br /> <br /> (Yes, I realize that's not how actually that power worked)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T00:08:23-07:00","id":464376,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if some contracts took advantage of God Machine infrastructure or some of the arcane physics that the GM uses to accomplish its goals; I doubt the GM has an infrastructure dedicated to making sure Changeling contracts work. I mean obviously this is all dependent on your ST having the GM in the game* I mean Demon is the only WOD game I'm aware of that would be exceptionally diminished if the GM were not a thing in the game. That being said the core book for Demon says that there is while some demons believe,or suspect that the GM has some connection to the contracts/pacts the fallen make there is no evidence that says so directly. As a result I'm thinking if Demons -who are explicitly designed by the GM- don't necessarily run their contract systems through the GM then the machine probably doesn't run the system for changeling contracts either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Am I the only one who's instincts just read that as &quot;The Storyteller might decide not to let the Game master in the game?&quot;**<br /> **Also am I the only one who finds that notion amusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T03:37:10-07:00","id":464492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/462895-do-contracts-work-because-of-the-god-machine#post462895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contracts work by inheriting greater than normal benefits due to occult agreements with aspects of reality and/or loopholes in this agreements that are exploited. Given that the God Machine is the arbiter and (arguably) the motive force behind how the universe works, is it reasonable to assume that the agreements are actually between something (Arcadia itself?) and the God Machine? If true, what are the implications of this? What's the metaphysical relationship between Contracts, Embeds and/or Exploits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. I kinda hate cross-over, but in the name of trying to be helpful, let's make an attempt.<br /> <br /> What if it were possible to actually storm Arcadia? It wouldn't be easy, but the first thing you'd have to do is shift your perspective. Understand that Arcadia is basically a massive network of ancient Infrastructures cut loose from the G-M, running on a perverted form of Essence called Glamour. At first, maybe you'd recruit a Demon or two to help you figure things out. They get some Aether out of the deal; Aether that you can't use anyways. The trick is to find the places where the Keepers can't see, but are still Arcadia. The real Arcadia. The clockwork Gears. The mechanical Turk invisibly playing chess. Some Demons know how to find those; they know what to look for. You smash those and entire Realms cease to exist. Some of the True Fae flat-out dissolve on the spot; the fetches they made crumbling and the Changelings who escaped finding themselves still Mantled and Pledged, but without Contracts or Glamour. The consequences of even an incomplete, if massive, victory.<br /> <br /> But then you realize that the G-M is interested in helping you. It doesn't want Arcadia around anymore. Making Changelings is a problem for it: sometimes the abducted were necessary pieces for a matrix. Sometimes it fails to notice that its matrix has been disrupted by a replacement fetch and everything comes crashing down. A Messenger Angel gives advice to one of your friends on how to re-insert himself into his old life. A Guardian Angel shows up when you're cornered by your Keeper. This G-M: it's being helpful. It's being trustworthy. Maybe you should do this. Break Arcadia itself. Sacrifice a Demon's trust to gain the G-M's. It offers to crack you open, unlock the sixth dot of a Contract: an Exploit. No fairy catch to it: merely that your mask shudders from its use. Do you take that gift?<br /> <br /> Of course, what you don't know is that the G-M is ready to betray you. It perceives the Keepers as creating half-angel, half-human hybrids. It's smart. It knows what the root of the problem is. But once the root is destroyed, there's still the matter of clean-up. If you find out, is saving your skin worth allowing Arcadia, all the suffering Changelings, all the Changelings-to-be, to keep going? Is saving all the Changelings who have already escaped once worth the inevitable creation of more? And what do the Demon rings think of all this? Is a Saboteur going to decide that Changelings need to therefore die? It doesn't see that you're trying to break a piece of the G-M; it sees that you're a product of the G-M, indirect and much-removed, but a product and thus inevitably part of its ineffable plan. Is an Integrator going to try to re-connect Arcadia to the G-M, re-assert its control, rather than see it destroyed? What if some of the Changelings are helping it? They were promised that their Contracts would be restored by such an act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}